<section class="container page-head">
  <p class="hero-kicker">Our vision</p>
  <h1>Not a catalog.<br>A connected story.</h1>
  <p class="hook">
    AntarikshPedia exists so anyone can understand space exploration the way
    it actually happened — a web of missions, machines, people, ideas, and
    world events shaping one another.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="container mp-section reveal">
  <div class="section-head"><h2>One knowledge network</h2><span class="mono-tag">the model</span></div>
  <ol class="chain" role="list">
    {% for step in ['Agency', 'Program', 'Mission', 'Spacecraft', 'Instruments', 'Events', 'Discoveries', 'Publications'] %}
      <li>{{ step }}</li>{% if not loop.last %}<li aria-hidden="true" class="chain-arrow">→</li>{% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>
</section>

<section class="container mp-section reveal">
  <div class="section-head"><h2>How it grows</h2><span class="mono-tag">roadmap</span></div>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <article class="principle-card now">
      <span class="phase-tag">Phase 1 — now</span>
      <h3>Pages for everything in the record</h3>
      <p>A page per mission, agency, and country — generated from one
         canonical dataset, cross-linked automatically.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="principle-card">
      <span class="phase-tag">Phase 2 — depth</span>
      <h3>Stories, sources, media</h3>
      <p>Long-form mission histories with verified launch details,
         license-checked imagery, and traceable citations.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="principle-card">
      <span class="phase-tag">Phase 3 — community</span>
      <h3>Reviewed contributions</h3>
      <p>Public corrections and additions staged as pending until a reviewer
         approves them against a cited source.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container mp-section reveal standard">
  <blockquote>
    Separate sourced fact from interpretation. Present history with clear
    attribution, neutral language, and links to credible sources.
  </blockquote>
  <p class="standard-note">Every AntarikshPedia page is held to this standard.</p>
  <a class="btn btn-solid" href="/timeline/">Turn to page one</a>
</section>
